course: dictionary
lesson: 879
title: Too much, all at once
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A binge means doing too much of something in a short time. You can binge on food, drinks or TV. Binge is a verb (to binge) and a noun (a binge), so it can describe what someone does or a time when they did too much.
explain: «Binge-watching a whole series in one weekend, with little sleep and no fresh air, can make you feel tired and strange the next day.» The clues are whole series, one weekend and little sleep. Those words tell you there was far too much, all at once. Check your meaning by swapping it in: watching too many episodes in a short time still makes sense.
explain: In health lessons, binge eating and binge drinking are described as unhealthy. If you ever worry about your eating or drinking, or someone else's, talk to a trusted adult or a doctor.
fact: «Binge» means to do too much of something in a short time.
fact: «Binge-watch» is informal and means watching many episodes of a show one after another.
fact: As a noun, «a chocolate binge» is one short time of eating far too much chocolate.
fact: Binge eating and binge drinking are unhealthy, and a trusted adult or doctor can help.
fact: Context clues for «binge» include words like whole, too much, one weekend and all at once.
exercise: «Binge-watching a whole series in one weekend, with little sleep and no fresh air, can make you feel tired and strange the next day.» What does binge-watching mean? | *Watching many episodes of a show one after another | Watching a single short video once | Watching the weather forecast on the news | Watching birds in the garden
exercise: «He had a chocolate binge after the party.» What does binge mean in this sentence? | A kind of chocolate cake | *A short time of having far too much chocolate | A long walk to the shop for chocolate | A tiny taste of one chocolate sweet
exercise: Why are binge eating and binge drinking described as unhealthy in health lessons? | Because only adults are allowed to do them | Because they make you grow taller | *Because they mean doing too much, all at once | Because they are a kind of sport
test: Which word means to do too much of something in a short time? | *Binge | Measure | Stroll | Relax
test: Which clue in «Binge-watching a whole series in one weekend, with little sleep and no fresh air, can make you feel tired and strange the next day.» shows there was too much? | *A whole series in one weekend | Feeling strange | The next day | Fresh air
exam: Which best describes binge? | Doing a little of something, slowly, every day | *Doing too much of something, all at once | Drawing pictures of your favourite things | Sleeping for a very long time
